language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ birthday_coins: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Tommy was given 15 coins for his birthday. Each coin is a half-crown, a shilling or a sixpence, but he was not necessarily given coins of all three kinds. When he added them up he had 1 pound, 5 shillings and 6 pence. How many half-crowns could he have been given? Old British money: a pound is 20 shillings and a shilling is 12 pence, so a pound is 240 pence; a half-crown is 30 pence, a shilling 12 pence and a sixpence 6 pence.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/birthday_coins.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ half_crowns: the number of half-crowns given
find half_crowns : int(0..15)
$ shillings: the number of shillings given (auxiliary)
find shillings : int(0..15)
$ sixpences: the number of sixpences given (auxiliary)
find sixpences : int(0..15)

such that
$ he was given 15 coins in all
half_crowns + shillings + sixpences = 15,
$ the coins add up to 1 pound, 5 shillings and 6 pence, which is 306 pence
30 * half_crowns + 12 * shillings + 6 * sixpences = 306
